# Policy for .clang-tidy file maintenance:
#  - all checks from https://releases.llvm.org/22.1.0/tools/clang/tools/extra/docs/clang-tidy/checks/list.html should be listed here
#  - no regex usage, only explicit enable/disable
#  - if a check is disabled an explicit reason should be specified
Checks:                                                      #(status)(offer_fixes)(description)
  - 'bugprone-argument-comment'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Checks that argument comments at call sites match the parameter names in the declaration.)
  - 'bugprone-assert-side-effect'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags expressions with side effects inside assert() macros that disappear in release builds.)
  - 'bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition'                    #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on assignments (=) inside if conditions where equality (==) was likely intended.)
  - 'bugprone-bad-signal-to-kill-thread'                     #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags invalid or dangerous signal numbers passed to thread termination functions.)
  - 'bugprone-bitwise-pointer-cast'                          #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects unsafe pointer casting performed via bitwise operations.)
  - 'bugprone-bool-pointer-implicit-conversion'              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Flags implicit conversions from boolean pointers to boolean values in conditions.)
  - 'bugprone-capturing-this-in-member-variable'             #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when a lambda captures this by value inside a member variable initializer.)
  - 'bugprone-casting-through-void'                          #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags dangerous double-casting through void* that bypasses type checking.)
  - 'bugprone-chained-comparison'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags chained comparisons like a < b < c which evaluate unexpectedly in C++.)
  - 'bugprone-command-processor'                             #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on usage of system() due to vulnerability to command injection bugs.)
  - 'bugprone-compare-pointer-to-member-virtual-function'    #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns against comparing pointers to virtual member functions.)
  - 'bugprone-copy-constructor-init'                         #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects copy constructors that fail to initialize base classes or member fields.)
  - 'bugprone-copy-constructor-mutates-argument'             #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags copy constructors that accept non-const references and modify their argument.)
  - 'bugprone-dangling-handle'                               #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on dangling handles (like std::string_view) constructed from temporary objects.)
  - 'bugprone-default-operator-new-on-overaligned-type'      #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when standard operator new is called on over-aligned types.)
  - 'bugprone-dynamic-static-initializers'                   #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects dynamic initialization of static variables across translation units.)
  - 'bugprone-empty-catch'                                   #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags empty catch blocks that swallow exceptions without handling them.)
  - 'bugprone-exception-copy-constructor-throws'             #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags exception class copy constructors that can throw exception types.)
  - 'bugprone-exception-escape'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,"Detects exceptions escaping from noexcept functions, destructors, or main().")
  - 'bugprone-float-loop-counter'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on floating-point variables used as loop counters due to accumulation errors.)
  - 'bugprone-fold-init-type'                                #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when the initial value type in std::accumulate or std::reduce causes truncation or precision loss.)
  - 'bugprone-forward-declaration-namespace'                 #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects forward declarations located in mismatched or incorrect namespaces.)
  - 'bugprone-forwarding-reference-overload'                 #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on constructors taking universal forwarding references that shadow copy/move constructors.)
  - 'bugprone-inaccurate-erase'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Flags calls to std::remove or std::remove_if whose return values are not passed to erase().)
  - 'bugprone-inc-dec-in-conditions'                         #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on increment or decrement operations inside loop or conditional expressions.)
  - 'bugprone-incorrect-enable-if'                           #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects incorrect usages of std::enable_if (such as missing ::type).)
  - 'bugprone-incorrect-enable-shared-from-this'             #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Flags classes that inherit from std::enable_shared_from_this with wrong template types or non-public inheritance.)
  - 'bugprone-incorrect-roundings'                           #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on bad floating-point rounding patterns like (int)(x + 0.5) for negative numbers.)
  - 'bugprone-infinite-loop'                                 #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Finds loops whose exit conditions can never be reached or modified.)
  - 'bugprone-integer-division'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects integer division operations where floating-point results were likely expected.)
  - 'bugprone-invalid-enum-default-initialization'           #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on uninitialized enum variables or invalid default enum values.)
  - 'bugprone-macro-parentheses'                             #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns when macro parameters or entire macro expressions are missing enclosing parentheses.)
  - 'bugprone-macro-repeated-side-effects'                   #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects macro parameters with side effects that are evaluated multiple times.)
  - 'bugprone-misleading-setter-of-reference'                #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on setter methods taking references that bind to temporary objects instead of storing the reference.)
  - 'bugprone-misplaced-operator-in-strlen-in-alloc'         #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,"Detects addition operators misplaced inside strlen() during memory allocation calls (e.g., malloc(strlen(s + 1))).")
  - 'bugprone-misplaced-pointer-arithmetic-in-alloc'         #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns on pointer arithmetic incorrectly applied inside allocation size arguments.)
  - 'bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast'                       #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,"Finds widening casts placed inside expressions rather than outside, leading to truncation before casting.")
  - 'bugprone-move-forwarding-reference'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects std::move used on forwarding references instead of std::forward.)
  - 'bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion'       #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects dangerous implicit multi-level pointer-to-pointer conversions.)
  - 'bugprone-multiple-new-in-one-expression'                #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags multiple new allocations in a single statement that risk memory leaks on exception throwing.)
  - 'bugprone-multiple-statement-macro'                      #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags multi-statement macros that are not enclosed in a do { ... } while(0) block.)
  - 'bugprone-no-escape'                                     #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Ensures parameters marked __attribute__((noescape)) do not escape the function scope.)
  - 'bugprone-non-zero-enum-to-bool-conversion'              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when converting enums without a zero value directly to bool.)
  - 'bugprone-nondeterministic-pointer-iteration-order'      #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,"Warns on iteration over pointer containers with non-deterministic ordering (e.g., std::unordered_set<T*>).")
  - 'bugprone-not-null-terminated-result'                    #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns when string operations like memcpy or strncpy do not guarantee null termination.)
  - 'bugprone-optional-value-conversion'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects unsafe or redundant value conversions on std::optional objects.)
  - 'bugprone-parent-virtual-call'                           #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Finds qualified virtual function calls using explicit parent class names that bypass virtual dispatch.)
  - 'bugprone-pointer-arithmetic-on-polymorphic-object'      #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on pointer arithmetic performed on pointers to polymorphic classes.)
  - 'bugprone-posix-return'                                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects incorrect checks on POSIX function returns that compare directly against negative values instead of -1.)
  - 'bugprone-random-generator-seed'                         #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags pseudo-random number generators seeded with predictable or default values.)
  - 'bugprone-raw-memory-call-on-non-trivial-type'           #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,"Flags raw memory operations (memset, memcpy) applied to non-trivially copyable types.")
  - 'bugprone-redundant-branch-condition'                    #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns on branch conditions that are redundant due to enclosing conditional statements.)
  - 'bugprone-reserved-identifier'                           #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,"Flags usage of reserved language identifiers (e.g., starting with double underscores).")
  - 'bugprone-return-const-ref-from-parameter'               #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Finds functions returning const references to local temporaries or parameters passed by value.)
  - 'bugprone-shared-ptr-array-mismatch'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns when std::shared_ptr manages array objects without using the array delete/type specifier.)
  - 'bugprone-signal-handler'                                #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags calls to non-async-signal-safe functions inside signal handling routines.)
  - 'bugprone-signed-char-misuse'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects signed char used in arithmetic operations or array indexing where signedness causes issues.)
  - 'bugprone-sizeof-container'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when sizeof() is applied to standard container objects instead of element types.)
  - 'bugprone-sizeof-expression'                             #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects suspicious or incorrect usage patterns of the sizeof operator.)
  - 'bugprone-spuriously-wake-up-functions'                  #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when condition variable wait() operations are called outside of condition loops.)
  - 'bugprone-standalone-empty'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects calls to .empty() on containers where the returned boolean is ignored.)
  - 'bugprone-std-namespace-modification'                    #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when adding custom declarations or definitions directly into the std namespace.)
  - 'bugprone-string-constructor'                            #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects suspicious std::string constructor arguments (such as swapping length and character arguments).)
  - 'bugprone-string-integer-assignment'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns when assigning an integer to std::string where character conversion was likely intended.)
  - 'bugprone-string-literal-with-embedded-nul'              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags string literals containing embedded NUL characters (\0).)
  - 'bugprone-stringview-nullptr'                            #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects construction of std::string_view from a nullptr.)
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-enum-usage'                         #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags suspicious bitwise and arithmetic operations on enum values.)
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-include'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when #include directives include .c or .cpp implementation files instead of headers.)
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-memset-usage'                       #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Flags memset calls with swapped parameters or zero size arguments.)
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-missing-comma'                      #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects missing commas between elements in string arrays that cause unintended string concatenation.)
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-realloc-usage'                      #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,"Warns when realloc returns directly to the original pointer, risking memory leaks on failure.")
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-semicolon'                          #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,"Detects misplaced semicolons immediately following if, for, or while conditions.")
  - 'bugprone-suspicious-stringview-data-usage'              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when passing .data() of std::string_view to APIs expecting null-terminated strings.)
  - 'bugprone-swapped-arguments'                             #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Identifies function calls where argument positions appear accidentally swapped relative to parameter types.)
  - 'bugprone-tagged-union-member-count'                     #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Flags discrepancies between tag enum member count and union field count in tagged unions.)
  - 'bugprone-terminating-continue'                          #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns on continue statements in single-iteration loops that prematurely terminate execution.)
  - 'bugprone-throw-keyword-missing'                         #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when creating an exception object without executing the throw keyword.)
  - 'bugprone-too-small-loop-variable'                       #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns when loop counter types are too narrow to reach the upper bound loop limit.)
  - 'bugprone-unchecked-optional-access'                     #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects dereferences of std::optional without prior has_value() checks.)
  - 'bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion'         #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects unchecked string-to-number parsing functions (like atoi) lacking error handling.)
  - 'bugprone-undefined-memory-manipulation'                 #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on raw memory operations on types that are not trivially copyable or setup.)
  - 'bugprone-undelegated-constructor'                       #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Detects constructors that instantiate temporary instances of their own class instead of delegating.)
  - 'bugprone-unhandled-exception-at-new'                    #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on raw new operations where std::bad_alloc is not caught or handled.)
  - 'bugprone-unintended-char-ostream-output'                #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Flags unintended character integer values output to stream operators as characters instead of numbers.)
  - 'bugprone-unique-ptr-array-mismatch'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns when std::unique_ptr manages array allocations using non-array delete/type.)
  - 'bugprone-unsafe-functions'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,"Flags usage of functions declared unsafe (e.g., strcpy, gets) and suggests safe alternatives.")
  - 'bugprone-unused-raii'                                   #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Warns on anonymous temporary RAII objects that are destroyed immediately upon creation.)
  - 'bugprone-use-after-move'                                #(ENABLED)(No)(Bugprone,Warns on reading or accessing objects whose values have already been moved away.)
  - 'bugprone-virtual-near-miss'                             #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Bugprone,Detects derived class virtual methods that almost—but do not strictly—match base class signatures.)
  - 'cert-err33-c'                                           #(ENABLED)(No)(CERT,Checks that return values of error-prone standard C functions are checked.)
  - 'cert-err60-cpp'                                         #(ENABLED)(No)(CERT,Ensures exception objects thrown are throw-copy-constructible.)
  - 'cert-flp30-c'                                           #(ENABLED)(No)(CERT,Warns against using floating-point variables as loop counters.)
  - 'cert-msc50-cpp'                                         #(ENABLED)(No)(CERT,Warns against pseudo-random number generators seeded with weak or predictable values.)
  - 'cert-oop58-cpp'                                         #(ENABLED)(No)(CERT,Ensures copy assignment and copy constructors do not mutate the source object being copied.)
  - 'concurrency-thread-canceltype-asynchronous'             #(ENABLED)(No)(Concurrency,Warns against setting thread cancellation type to PTHREAD_CANCEL_ASYNCHRONOUS.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-avoid-capturing-lambda-coroutines'    #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Warns against capturing variables by reference inside coroutine lambdas.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-avoid-goto'                           #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Discourages the use of goto statements.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-avoid-reference-coroutine-parameters' #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Flags reference parameters passed to coroutines that risk dangling after suspension.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-init-variables'                       #(ENABLED)(Yes)(CppCoreGuidelines,Ensures all local variables are explicitly initialized at declaration.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-interfaces-global-init'               #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Prevents global variable initializations from depending on uninitialized static state in other units.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-misleading-capture-default-by-value'  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(CppCoreGuidelines,Warns on default-by-value captures [=] in lambdas when this is implicitly captured by reference.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-no-suspend-with-lock'                 #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Warns when suspending a coroutine while holding a lock.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-prefer-member-initializer'            #(ENABLED)(Yes)(CppCoreGuidelines,Prefers member initializers in constructor init-lists over assignment in constructor bodies.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast'                 #(ENABLED)(Yes)(CppCoreGuidelines,Flags C-style casts in favor of modern C++ casts.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast'        #(ENABLED)(Yes)(CppCoreGuidelines,Warns against using static_cast for downcasting polymorphic types.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-rvalue-reference-param-not-moved'     #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Flags rvalue reference parameters that are never moved or forwarded inside function bodies.)
  - 'cppcoreguidelines-slicing'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(CppCoreGuidelines,Detects object slicing when assigning or passing derived instances as base objects.)
  - 'hicpp-exception-baseclass'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(HICPP,Ensures custom exception classes inherit publicly from std::exception.)
  - 'hicpp-ignored-remove-result'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(HICPP,"Flags ignored return values of std::remove, std::remove_if, and std::unique.")
  - 'hicpp-no-assembler'                                     #(ENABLED)(No)(HICPP,Warns on inline assembly usage (__asm__ or asm).)
  - 'linuxkernel-must-check-errs'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(LinuxKernel,Checks that Linux kernel error-returning functions have their return values handled using IS_ERR() or similar macros.)
  - 'misc-anonymous-namespace-in-header'                     #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Warns when anonymous namespaces appear inside header files.)
  - 'misc-confusable-identifiers'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Detects identifiers containing visually similar or confusable Unicode characters.)
  - 'misc-coroutine-hostile-raii'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Flags RAII objects spanning coroutine suspension points that risk locks or deadlocks.)
  - 'misc-definitions-in-headers'                            #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Misc,Detects non-inline function or variable definitions placed inside header files.)
  - 'misc-header-include-cycle'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Flags circular #include dependency loops between header files.)
  - 'misc-misleading-bidirectional'                          #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Warns on bidirectional Unicode control characters that alter visual code execution order.)
  - 'misc-misleading-identifier'                             #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Warns on identifiers using confusing combinations of lookalike characters.)
  - 'misc-misplaced-const'                                   #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Detects const applied to typedefs/aliases in ways that modify pointer constness unexpectedly.)
  - 'misc-new-delete-overloads'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Ensures custom operator new overloads have corresponding operator delete overloads.)
  - 'misc-non-copyable-objects'                              #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Detects instances of non-copyable objects passed or returned by value.)
  - 'misc-predictable-rand'                                  #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Warns on calls to rand() or pseudo-random functions lacking secure seeding.)
  - 'misc-redundant-expression'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Misc,"Detects redundant or tautological expressions (e.g., x == x, x | 0).")
  - 'misc-static-assert'                                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Misc,Replaces runtime assertions evaluated with compile-time constant expressions with static_assert.)
  - 'misc-throw-by-value-catch-by-reference'                 #(ENABLED)(No)(Misc,Ensures exceptions are thrown by value and caught by reference.)
  - 'misc-uniqueptr-reset-release'                           #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Misc,Replaces x.reset(y.release()) with x = std::move(y).)
  - 'misc-unused-alias-decls'                                #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Misc,Detects unused type aliases (using or typedef declarations).)
  - 'misc-unused-using-decls'                                #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Misc,Flags unused using declarations in source files.)
  - 'modernize-avoid-bind'                                   #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces std::bind calls with standard C++ lambdas.)
  - 'modernize-avoid-setjmp-longjmp'                         #(ENABLED)(No)(Modernize,Discourages using setjmp and longjmp in C++ code.)
  - 'modernize-deprecated-ios-base-aliases'                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces deprecated std::ios_base stream aliases with modern equivalents.)
  - 'modernize-loop-convert'                                 #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Converts index- or iterator-based loops into C++11 range-based for loops.)
  - 'modernize-macro-to-enum'                                #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces #define constants with enum or enum class.)
  - 'modernize-make-shared'                                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces raw new operations inside std::shared_ptr constructions with std::make_shared.)
  - 'modernize-make-unique'                                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces raw new operations inside std::unique_ptr constructions with std::make_unique.)
  - 'modernize-min-max-use-initializer-list'                 #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces nested std::min/std::max calls with initializer list overloads.)
  - 'modernize-raw-string-literal'                           #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,"Converts escaped string literals into C++11 raw string literals (R""(...)"").")
  - 'modernize-replace-auto-ptr'                             #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces deprecated std::auto_ptr with std::unique_ptr.)
  - 'modernize-replace-disallow-copy-and-assign-macro'       #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces DISALLOW_COPY_AND_ASSIGN macros with deleted special member functions (= delete).)
  - 'modernize-replace-random-shuffle'                       #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces deprecated std::random_shuffle with std::shuffle.)
  - 'modernize-shrink-to-fit'                                #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces the vector(...).swap(...) idiom with standard .shrink_to_fit().)
  - 'modernize-unary-static-assert'                          #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces redundant two-argument static_assert calls with C++17 single-argument static_assert.)
  - 'modernize-use-auto'                                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces explicit type declarations with auto where types are redundant or verbose.)
  - 'modernize-use-bool-literals'                            #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,"Replaces integer literals (0, 1) in boolean contexts with true or false.")
  - 'modernize-use-constraints'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces SFINAE / std::enable_if constructs with C++20 requires clauses and concepts.)
  - 'modernize-use-designated-initializers'                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Suggests using C++20 designated initializers for struct construction.)
  - 'modernize-use-emplace'                                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces push_back/insert calls with emplace_back/emplace to avoid temporary object creation.)
  - 'modernize-use-equals-delete'                            #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces un-implemented private special member functions with = delete.)
  - 'modernize-use-integer-sign-comparison'                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces signed/unsigned comparison logic with C++20 std::cmp_* utilities.)
  - 'modernize-use-noexcept'                                 #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Adds explicit noexcept specifiers to functions that do not throw exceptions.)
  - 'modernize-use-ranges'                                   #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces standard algorithm calls with C++20 std::ranges equivalents.)
  - 'modernize-use-scoped-lock'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces std::lock_guard with C++17 std::scoped_lock.)
  - 'modernize-use-starts-ends-with'                         #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces find or substr comparisons with C++20 std::string::starts_with and ends_with.)
  - 'modernize-use-std-format'                               #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,"Replaces sprintf, ostringstream, or absl::StrFormat with C++20 std::format.")
  - 'modernize-use-std-numbers'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces hardcoded mathematical constants with standard C++20 <numbers> constants.)
  - 'modernize-use-std-print'                                #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces printf or std::cout stream calls with C++23 std::print or std::println.)
  - 'modernize-use-transparent-functors'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,"Replaces standard comparator functors with transparent versions (e.g., std::less<>()).")
  - 'modernize-use-uncaught-exceptions'                      #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces deprecated std::uncaught_exception with C++17 std::uncaught_exceptions.)
  - 'modernize-use-using'                                    #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Modernize,Replaces legacy typedef declarations with modern C++ using type aliases.)
  - 'mpi-buffer-deref'                                       #(ENABLED)(Yes)(MPI,Ensures buffer pointers passed to MPI functions are correctly passed and dereferenced.)
  - 'mpi-type-mismatch'                                      #(ENABLED)(Yes)(MPI,Flags type mismatches between underlying buffer types and MPI_Datatype arguments.)
  - 'performance-faster-string-find'                         #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Replaces single-character string literal arguments in find calls with character literals.)
  - 'performance-for-range-copy'                             #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Detects range-based for loop variables initialized by value causing accidental copies.)
  - 'performance-implicit-conversion-in-loop'                #(ENABLED)(No)(Performance,Warns on implicit type conversions of range-loop variables in each iteration.)
  - 'performance-inefficient-algorithm'                      #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Replaces generic STL algorithms on associative containers with faster container member functions.)
  - 'performance-inefficient-string-concatenation'           #(ENABLED)(No)(Performance,Flags repeated string concatenation in loops using the + operator.)
  - 'performance-inefficient-vector-operation'               #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Detects vector allocations or push_back calls in loops that should reserve space upfront.)
  - 'performance-move-constructor-init'                      #(ENABLED)(No)(Performance,Ensures move constructors initialize base classes and members using move semantics rather than copy.)
  - 'performance-no-automatic-move'                          #(ENABLED)(No)(Performance,Identifies return statements where automatic move construction is prevented (e.g. returning const locals).)
  - 'performance-noexcept-destructor'                        #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Recommends marking destructors as noexcept to avoid runtime performance overhead.)
  - 'performance-noexcept-swap'                              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Ensures custom swap functions are explicitly marked noexcept.)
  - 'performance-trivially-destructible'                     #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Warns when user-defined destructors prevent classes with trivial members from being trivially destructible.)
  - 'performance-type-promotion-in-math-fn'                  #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Performance,Detects float parameters implicitly promoted to double when calling standard math functions.)
  - 'portability-restrict-system-includes'                   #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Portability,Restricts inclusion of system headers that vary across target platforms.)
  - 'portability-simd-intrinsics'                            #(ENABLED)(No)(Portability,Flags architecture-specific SIMD intrinsic calls that limit portability.)
  - 'portability-std-allocator-const'                        #(ENABLED)(No)(Portability,Flags deprecated std::allocator<const T> instantiations.)
  - 'portability-template-virtual-member-function'           #(ENABLED)(No)(Portability,Warns against virtual member functions in class templates that impair cross-compiler ABI compatibility.)
  - 'readability-ambiguous-smartptr-reset-call'              #(ENABLED)(Yes)(Readability,Clarifies ambiguous smart pointer .reset() calls where passing nullptr clarifies intent.)
